WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Drop a small piece of sodium into water.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.410
It floats, melts into a ball,
and fizzes about the surface.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.730
Caesium sits further down group 1.

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.990
Drop it into cold water, and it explodes.

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.650
Same group, same kind of reaction,
wildly different results.

6
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.750
So why does sodium fizz on
water while caesium explodes?

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.930
In this mission, you'll write equations
for group 1 metals reacting with water,

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.830
and find out why reactivity
changes down the group.

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.810
Then you'll watch halogens
displace one another from solution,

10
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.250
and see the opposite trend in group 17.

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.560
Your mission: explain why caesium reacts
so much more violently than sodium.
